{
  "title": [
    "fiddle~",
    "fiddle"
  ],
  "description": "peak number, frequency and amplitude",
  "origin": "vanilla",
  "categories": [
    "Analysis"
  ],
  "inlets": [
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "signal",
          "description": "signal input to be analyzed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bang",
          "description": "poll current values when auto mode is off"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    }
  ],
  "outlets": [
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "float",
          "description": "cooked pitch output"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    },
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "bang",
          "description": "a bang is sent on new attacks"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    },
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "description": "continuous raw pitch and amplitude"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    },
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "float",
          "description": "amplitude in dB"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    },
    {
      "messages": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "description": "peak number, frequency and amplitude (4th argument nonzero)"
        }
      ],
      "repeat": false
    }
  ],
  "arguments": [
    {
      "type": "float",
      "description": "window size",
      "default": "1024"
    },
    {
      "type": "float",
      "description": "number of pitch outlets",
      "default": "1"
    },
    {
      "type": "float",
      "description": "number of peaks to find",
      "default": "20"
    },
    {
      "type": "float",
      "description": "number of peaks to output",
      "default": "0"
    }
  ],
  "flags": [],
  "methods": [
    {
      "type": "amp-range <float, float>",
      "description": "set low and high amplitude threshold"
    },
    {
      "type": "vibrato <float, float>",
      "description": "set period in ms and pitch deviation for \"cooked\" pitch outlet"
    },
    {
      "type": "reattack <float, float>",
      "description": "set period in ms and amplitude in dB to report re-attack"
    },
    {
      "type": "auto <float>",
      "description": "nonzero sets to auto mode (default) and zero sets it off"
    },
    {
      "type": "npartial <float>",
      "description": "set partial number to be weighted half as strongly as the fundamental"
    },
    {
      "type": "npoints <float>",
      "description": "sets number of points in analysis window"
    },
    {
      "type": "print",
      "description": "print out settings"
    }
  ],
  "body": "[fiddle~] estimates the pitch and amplitude of an incoming sound, both continuously and as a stream of discrete note events, and reports attacks. It can also output the sinusoidal peaks it found in the spectrum. The arguments set the window size, the number of pitches to look for, the number of peaks to consider and the number of peaks to output."
}